315 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This project is part of the collaboration between the Higher Institute of Electronics and Digital \(ISEN\) and the Federal University of Ouro Preto \(UFOP\). It is part of a major research initiative carried out under the direction of Professor Carlos Henrique Gomes Ferreira, which aims to explore the dynamics of discussions around electronic cigarettes in several countries, with a particular focus on France. The objective is to understand how electronic cigarettes are perceived, debated and understood in different cultural and regulatory contexts.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
316 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (A first part of the work has already been carried out for Brazil, in Portuguese, as well as in English. The analysis of these speeches revealed interesting specificities depending on the linguistic and cultural contexts. Continuing this approach, we have chosen to concentrate our efforts on the French part in order to complete this comparative study. The French part of the research focuses on the collection and analysis of data from video content platforms, in particular YouTube, which offers a rich source of information on perceptions and public debates around electronic cigarettes.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
317 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This project is also part of the perspective of a scientific publication. The objective is to produce an article that will contribute to the scientific literature on perceptions and debates relating to electronic cigarettes around the world. This publication aims to share our results with the international scientific community, while informing policy makers and health professionals of current dynamics in this area.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
318 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (During this internship, I worked closely with another student, adopting a collaborative approach at every stage of the project: from collecting data via YouTube to analyzing and interpreting it. This collaboration was crucial to comprehensively address the complex discourse surrounding electronic cigarettes, particularly in France. Together, we developed a robust dataset, based on videos, comments, and online discussions, which will be used not only for current research, but also for future studies. This work will contribute to a better understanding of the impact of electronic cigarettes in different national contexts.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
319 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (In summary, this project represents a significant contribution to research on electronic cigarettes, taking into account the cultural and regulatory specificities of each country studied. It also paves the way for scientific publications that could influence public policies and public health strategies internationally.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
