326 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The technical objective of this project is to constitute a relevant and representative dataset of the perceptions and attitudes of the French public towards electronic cigarettes, by exploiting comments generated by users on the YouTube platform. To achieve this goal, it is essential to collect rich qualitative data, reflecting the diversity of opinions, personal experiences and discussions surrounding e-cigarettes, using a systematic and rigorous method.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
327 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The approach adopted is based on the use of a YouTube V3 API coupled with a personalized crawler, which makes it possible to collect comments related to electronic cigarettes in a targeted manner. The first step is to identify and extract relevant comments using a list of carefully selected keywords. These keywords should cover a wide range of terms associated with e-cigarettes, including popular brands, technical terms relating to the devices, as well as common expressions and synonyms related to nicotine consumption and health debates.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
328 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The data collection period extends from 2018 to the end of 2023, a period long enough to capture changes in public discourse and identify emerging trends. The objective is to create an exhaustive and reliable database, which can serve as a basis for subsequent studies on perceptions of electronic cigarettes in France. This database will not only paint a general picture of public opinions, but also reveal recurring concerns and nuances in discussions, such as risk perceptions, personal experiences, and attitudes towards regulations in force. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
329 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Thus, the ultimate goal is to have a robust dataset, capable of providing valuable insights for in-depth analyzes and contributing to a better understanding of how e-cigarettes are perceived and debated in the French context.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
