336 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The technical objective of the data cleaning phase is to ensure that the dataset collected from YouTube comments on e-cigarettes is of high quality, relevant, and specifically adapted to the analysis of perceptions in France. To achieve this, several stages of rigorous filtering and cleaning are implemented to ensure that the final data accurately reflects opinions and discussions relevant to our research topic.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
337 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The first step is to detect and remove duplicate comments, in order to avoid any distortion of the results which could skew the analysis by amplifying the frequency of certain points of view. Next, it is crucial to filter off-topic comments and videos, i.e. those not directly related to e-cigarettes, using a combination of prohibited keywords to eliminate irrelevant content, such as than advertisements or discussions about other products.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
338 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Once the video database has been cleaned, the next step is to ensure that all retained comments are in French. This is essential so that our artificial intelligence can work effectively on content exclusively in French. To achieve this goal, two AI models are used in tandem to filter comments: first the Roberta model, then a language detection model. These two models successively analyze each comment to identify those which are in French. Only comments validated by both AIs are included in the final dataset, reducing the risk of linguistic errors and ensuring that our analysis focuses only on French content.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
339 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (In short, the objective is to produce a cleaned, precise dataset, and specifically adapted to the analysis of perceptions of electronic cigarettes in France. This cleaning process, with its multiple verification steps, aims to create a solid and reliable database that will serve as a foundation for in-depth analyzes and future research.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
