352 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (In order to maximize the quality of the marking and, therefore, the accuracy of the training, this process was carried out by three different people. Each commenter annotated the same sample of 400 comments, ensuring that the annotations are consistent and reliable.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
353 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (To determine the final set of labels and minimize discrepancies between annotators, we used the Fleiss Kappa method. This statistical index indicates the degree of agreement between multiple raters on a data set, taking into account the likelihood that annotations are produced by chance. This method makes it possible to quantify the reliability of the annotations and ensure that the labeling file reflects a consensus between the annotators.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
