362 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Training a model of this type involves several subtleties and challenges:)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
363 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 932 0 R
/E (Data Bias: If the labeling file contains an imbalance in the number of favorable or unfavorable comments, the model risks becoming biased, favoring one polarity over the other. It is therefore crucial to maintain a balance in the training data set.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
364 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 933 0 R
/E (Linguistic Complexity: French comments may contain idiomatic expressions, sarcasm, or ambiguous wording that may be difficult to correctly interpret by an AI model. Training must therefore be sophisticated enough to capture these subtleties.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
365 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 934 0 R
/E (Overfitting: Another risk is that of overfitting, where the model becomes overfit to the training data and loses its ability to generalize to new feedback. This requires the use of regularization and cross-validation techniques to evaluate the model's performance on unseen data.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
366 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 935 0 R
/E (Evolution of Language: The language used in comments may evolve over time, with new expressions or terms appearing. The model must be regularly updated to incorporate these developments and remain relevant.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
