656 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This project, resulting from the collaboration between the Higher Institute of Electronics and Digital \(ISEN\) and the Federal University of Ouro Preto \(UFOP\), is part of an international research framework led by Professor Carlos Henrique Gomes Ferreira. The objective is to study the discursive dynamics around electronic cigarettes in several cultural and regulatory contexts, focusing particularly on France. The project is part of broader comparative work which already includes analyzes carried out in Brazil \(in Portuguese\) and in English-speaking countries.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
657 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The project was rigorously structured through different phases defined from the start of the process. A Gantt chart was created to visualize the key steps, including data collection, data analysis and reporting of results. Each step had specific deadlines, with a clear distribution of responsibilities among team members.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
658 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (One of the central aspects of this project was the collaboration with another student. This partnership enabled an efficient distribution of tasks, ranging from the collection of data from YouTube to its analysis. Collaboration was essential to comprehensively address the complex discourse around electronic cigarettes, particularly in the French context. Team work facilitated the exchange of ideas and strengthened the quality of the analyzes carried out, while guaranteeing methodological consistency with previous studies carried out in Brazil and in English-speaking countries.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
659 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Under the supervision of Professor Carlos, the project took place mainly remotely, due to university strikes in Brazil. This constraint required rigorous remote organization, with the use of online communication tools to guarantee coordination and monitoring of the project. Despite these obstacles, the work proceeded efficiently thanks to regular meetings and open communication channels with the supervisor.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
660 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Although the project was part of a larger research initiative, it was strongly framed, with specific expectations and a methodological framework defined from the start. This structure, although limiting in terms of freedom of action, made it possible to be part of a dynamic consistent with research carried out in other cultural and linguistic contexts. The objective was to produce comparable results, which guided the methodological choices throughout the project.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
661 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The project will result in the creation of a scientific article intended for publication. This article will contribute to the existing literature on perceptions and debates around electronic cigarettes around the world, taking into account the cultural and regulatory specificities of each country. Additionally, this project paves the way for future research by creating a robust dataset that can be reused for other comparative studies.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
